# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  .gitignore — security-first · repo is PUBLIC
#  Rule: ".env.example" is committed (template); ".env" is NEVER committed (real values).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Secrets & environment (real values) — MOST CRITICAL
.env
.env.*
# .env.example is the committed template (names + fake placeholders only)
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets/
credentials/
*credential*.json
*secret*.json
token.json
*token*.json

# Personal / local overrides
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
*.local.*

# Dependencies / build artifacts
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
__pycache__/
*.log

# Local data (keep raw/personal data out, even if mock)
/data/
*.sqlite
*.db

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Project-specific (tailored) ──
# Raw n8n exports — only the sanitized workflow is committed
n8n/**/*.json
# ⚠ These were three HAND-LISTED exceptions until 2026-09-13, and the fourth workflow
# (owner-actions, CP 6d-1) was silently NOT committable because nobody remembered to extend the list —
# the same stale-allow-list defect that `check-deploy-separation.sh` was written to close, repeated here.
# Suffix-matched now, so the next sanitized export inherits it. The deny above stays broad: only files
# the sanitize step itself produces (`*.sanitized.json`) come back, never a raw export.
!n8n/workflow.sanitized.json
!n8n/workflow.*.sanitized.json

# Real per-client config — only the .example is committed
config/client.config.json

# PII-containing test data (repo is PUBLIC — this is critical)
/test-data/
tests/**/real-*.*
tests/**/*.pii.*

# Local headless-render previews (temporary Playwright output — never committed)
design/mockups/preview/

# Scratch / working files (raw diffs, temp dumps — never committed)
scratchpad_diff.txt
*.scratch
scratch/

# n8n rollback snapshots — FULL export (real credential/base/table ids) → NEVER committed.
# These are the known-good restore points for refactor rollback (see docs/n8n-rollback.md).
n8n/.snapshots/
*.local.json

# NOTE: n8n/screenshots/ and design/mockups/ are NOT ignored (portfolio / vitrin assets).
# design/mockups/variants/ holds the DELIVERED Phase-1 surface mockups (landing, then
# widget + dashboard) — committed for Cowork to review from git.

# Build-time config bridge output — may contain a REAL client config (Phase 6)
web/site/config.generated.json
# Built snippet bundle — bakes in the production webhook URL (host is a redaction target).
# Regenerate with: npm run build -w @salon/snippet
web/site/public/barber-widget.js
# TypeScript incremental build artefact, produced by the `check`/`typecheck` scripts.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Next.js 16 auto-generates these agent-instruction files on dev/build (tool output, not our content).
# ⚠ These two lines named `web/site/` ONLY until 2026-09-13. `web/dashboard` is a second Next app and its
# first `npm run dev` dropped both files into a tree that had been clean — the pattern was a hand-written
# per-app list that did not grow when a new app did. Written per-workspace now, so the next app inherits it.
# ⚠ DELIBERATE TRADE-OFF, written down because it is not obvious: this ALSO hides a hand-written
# `web/<app>/CLAUDE.md` should anyone ever want one. Accepted — `next dev` recreates the generated
# file on every run, so a hand-written one at that path would be overwritten anyway. Directory-scoped
# instructions for this repo live in the root CLAUDE.md and `.claude/rules/`.
web/*/AGENTS.md
web/*/CLAUDE.md

# Playwright MCP scratch (page snapshots + console logs — can capture tokens/PII)
.playwright-mcp/
